      <h2 id="glance" style="margin-top:0">At a glance</h2>
      <ol class="stop-steps">
        <li><strong>Health link:</strong> in large cohort studies, lower grip strength is associated with higher mortality risk. That is an association, not a cause.</li>
        <li><strong>Clinical use:</strong> handgrip is a simple marker of overall muscle strength (Bohannon 2019).</li>
        <li><strong>Training:</strong> no trial shows that training grip changes health outcomes.</li>
        <li><strong>Testing:</strong> a dynamometer measures force in kg. A timed dead hang is a personal measure and a different test.</li>
